id: pm-jev-0s07
title: Name evaluation source failures and support local tracker reads without GitHub
description: "Classify gh source-inspection failures with redacted first-line diagnostics and exact recovery steps; exercise eval and calibrate against eligible local trackers without gh or git, preserve label eligibility and isolated public-source guards. Related implementation: pm-jev-82ip, pm-jev-hx9w, pm-jev-f4ba."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-20T09:59:36.702Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T10:43:04.184Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T09:59:48.900Z",codex-agent,"Inspected source loading: every accepted --from currently runs git and gh before the SDK read. Implementing named gh failures with recovery guidance and fake-executable regression coverage. Local-source eligibility clarification is pending because the current public-origin and visibility verification requires those tools."
  "2026-10-20T10:01:22.633Z",codex-agent,"Diagnostic regressions pass (2 tests). Behavioral revert of inspectSource alone makes the fake-gh regression fail (1 pass, 1 fail), with the original opaque Public tracker inspection failed (gh) message; restored implementation passes. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks pass."
  "2026-10-20T10:06:45.128Z",codex-agent,"The host command harness now surfaces expected actionable gh diagnostics for both eval and calibrate before model calls. Focused linked test command passes 3/3, and diagnostic module line/branch/function coverage is 100%. Local reads remain pending the eligibility decision: accepting arbitrary --from directories conflicts with existing public clone verification. No source eligibility checks have been changed."
  "2026-10-20T10:10:20.241Z",codex-agent,"Awaiting source-eligibility clarification before changing local reads: --from currently accepts only committed public fleet clones, and enforcing origin/visibility/commit needs git and GitHub. A direct local-tracker mode would change that trust rule; a trusted snapshot format would need an explicit contract. Diagnostics and 3 focused tests are implemented; inspectSource-only revert fails as required. Full isolated npm release check is running; no no-tool success proof, commit or PR has been completed."
  "2026-10-20T10:12:53.961Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator resolved eligibility: keep default verified public snapshots, add explicit --local-unverified for direct SDK-only tracker reads, mark all local evidence and receipts, and refuse public artifact publication. Implementing source and persistence boundaries plus no-tool and behavioral-revert regressions."
  "2026-10-20T10:20:36.630Z",codex-agent,"Implemented --local-unverified via direct certified SDK reads with opaque local identities. Reports, all observation arms, receipt and data entries are marked; local calibration returns its receipt without writing project settings. Default public source verification remains intact. Public input, artifact generation, release/prepack and fixture checks reject nested local evidence. Focused checks passed 7/7. Reverting runEvaluationCommand alone fails the no-gh/no-git regression; reverting assertPublicProvenance alone fails the publication/fixture regression. Both fixes restored; earlier inspectSource-only revert proof also failed as required."
  "2026-10-20T10:25:20.154Z",codex-agent,Separate strict health inspection found managed pm-github SDK 2026.10.20 versus pinned host 2026.10.15. This is outside the source-diagnostics change; dependency pins and extension configuration remain unchanged. A dedicated follow-up records the observed gate failure. Both release checks remain required and are evaluated separately from strict tracker health.
  "2026-10-20T10:31:56.140Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm release gate passed through linked test 3: 244 tests passed, zero failed; coverage is 5145/5145 lines and statements, 202/202 functions, 2064/2064 branches (100% in every measured dimension); all 22 required source files reported. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation passed at unchanged thresholds. Bun linked release gate is now running against the same source. Strict-health follow-up is pm-jev-v2la."
  "2026-10-20T10:42:16.269Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated Bun release gate also passed through linked test 4: 244/244 tests, zero failures; 5145/5145 lines and statements, 202/202 functions, 2064/2064 branches (100%); all 22 required source files reported. Both full release checks passed at unchanged thresholds, with zero duplication and zero production vulnerabilities. No functional source changes followed the npm pass. No-gh/no-git local evaluation/calibration and public artifact/fixture refusal tests pass; independent inspection, local opt-in and provenance-guard reverts each fail their regression. Default public eligibility remains intact. Ready for PR review; strict health remains separately affected by pm-jev-v2la. No merge or release."
  "2026-10-20T10:43:04.184Z",codex-agent,"Coverage-count correction to the preceding Bun result: Bun measured 2065/2065 branches; npm measured 2064/2064. Both are 100%; the test counts (244/244 per gate), lines/statements (5145/5145), functions (202/202), required source count (22) and all other pass results are unchanged."
